# Stage trees are GENERATED: stage_N = transformer(stage_N-1), reproducible by
#   PYTHONSAFEPATH=1 .venv/bin/python recon/refactor/driver.py materialize N
# and fully pinned by the committed MANIFEST.json (every input path + input
# SHA-256 + output SHA-256).  They are ~17 MB and ~1,800 relative symlinks each,
# which would swamp every diff for zero information.
#
# Committed instead, and deliberately: MANIFEST.json, PARITY_MAP.json,
# QUARANTINE.json -- the evidence that a stage produced what it says it produced.
stage_*/tree/
__pycache__/

# EXCEPTION, 2026-07-29: stage_09_call_cohesion/tree's REAL FILES are tracked so
# the finished refactor is browsable on GitHub without cloning and regenerating.
# The ~2,505 relative symlinks in that tree remain ignored -- only the 1,694 real
# files (~14 MB) are committed, i.e. the content the ladder actually produced.
#
# They were added with `git add -f`, so this ignore rule still applies to
# UNTRACKED paths there.  CONSEQUENCE: after `driver.py materialize 9`, edits to
# already-tracked files are picked up normally, but any NEWLY CREATED file will
# be silently ignored by `git add -A`.  To re-sync the tracked set:
#
#   find recon/refactor/stage_09_call_cohesion/tree -type f \
#        -not -path '*__pycache__*' -print0 | xargs -0 git add -f
#
# Stages 00-08 remain evidence-only (MANIFEST/PARITY_MAP/QUARANTINE/SIZE_GATE).
